---
import CaseLayout from '../../components/CaseLayout.astro';
---
<CaseLayout
  title="Magnet"
  description="Fridge magnet poetry, with friends."
  label="Personal Project // Web App"
  cover="/assets/projects/magnet/cover.webp"
  coverAlt="Magnet — fridge magnet poetry with friends"
  meta={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Solo, Design &amp; Build' },
    { label: 'Platform', value: 'Installable web app' },
  ]}
  action={{ label: 'Open Magnet at magnet.paramore.design', href: 'https://magnet.paramore.design' }}
>
  <p>
    <strong>Fridge magnet poetry &mdash; with friends.</strong>
  </p>


  <p>
    Another idea I had kicked around for years. The first generated version gave me a working
    board and very little feeling. Everything after that was design work: how a tile lifts when
    you take it, how a phrase settles into place, and what it looks like when someone else moves
    a word while you are still looking at it.
  </p>
</CaseLayout>
